{:edb/db-before-t 1315 :edb/db-after-t 1316 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534628 50 #inst "2026-10-12T05:11:37.635Z" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186129167 1038 #edb/ref 17592186429974 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186129168 1038 #edb/ref 17592186429975 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186339069 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region inside the circumference ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" 13194139534628 17592186045417 false] [17592186339069 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region inside the circumference ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186339069 1074 "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,x=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/09/0960063edcce8ccd55dc2f77147c4a4982645c180e8b998d7e520c65131ea045.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186339069 1074 "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,x=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/09/0960063edcce8ccd55dc2f77147c4a4982645c180e8b998d7e520c65131ea045.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139534628 17592186045417 false] [17592186339071 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" 13194139534628 17592186045417 false] [17592186339071 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186389594 1074 "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/1b/1bee7870760a7c267ca83806f04b3fa8b933891fa5e5524ce76ee09f2c7c98e0.png)" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186389594 1074 "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/1b/1bee7870760a7c267ca83806f04b3fa8b933891fa5e5524ce76ee09f2c7c98e0.png)" 13194139534628 17592186045417 false] [17592186429961 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429976 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429961 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429977 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429961 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429978 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429961 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429979 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429961 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429980 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429961 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429961 1045 "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429961 1046 #edb/ref 17592186429979 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429961 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429961 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050822 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429961 1053 #uuid "d57582b7-233f-54ba-bba8-bc7760d18c20" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429962 1080 "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le {e}^{x-1},\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\\}" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429962 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429962 1083 #uuid "177be529-dbfe-5550-a65b-a03b4c722a7b" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429963 1080 "None of the listed" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429963 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429963 1083 #uuid "1ad9fabe-6ac2-5a64-ad33-5fdd7127093f" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429964 1080 "images/78/781f679784282a55e4ff6b7a5537047ef2f45c8346cc9d1ed341407ecb8f8a38.png" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592