5dacd0b-ebeb-5ba4-b6db-4ab0dd2f71e0" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429971 1080 "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le {e}^{x-1},\\,0\\le x\\le 2\\}" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429971 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429971 1083 #uuid "dfdb17ab-530e-5006-a6b1-b68bfc5121a3" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429962 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429966 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429968 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429970 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429971 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429972 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429972 1077 "selection" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429972 1078 #edb/ref 17592186429966 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429972 1079 #uuid "d1839b45-678e-5716-ac62-7bfdda74ad68" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429973 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429963 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429973 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429964 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429973 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429965 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429973 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429967 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429973 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429969 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429973 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429973 1077 "selection" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429973 1078 #edb/ref 17592186429967 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429973 1079 #uuid "e615de10-cf5a-5071-a58d-94a8d37e22e4" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429974 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429973 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429974 1069 "q-72042" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429974 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429974 1071 "Which of the following is a type I region in two-dimensional space?" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429974 1072 #uuid "033e3725-7b31-599b-85d8-6c6f830b966d" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429974 1074 "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](images/00/00654c32dbc74614de9b6fdd0f39a5f7d4ecb6ccca0c642ab7ca4a2a8cfe1d89.png)" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429975 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429972 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429975 1069 "q-72344" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429975 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429975 1071 "![](images/40/4066b07ace047e9a7ce813ed70dd6648649a192d648ed810fa96b5146d2c5581.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type II region in two-dimensional space?" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429975 1072 #uuid "5cace0f5-d8d3-5cc8-93c4-64d577bf2d3c" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429975 1074 "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x-1}\\,⟹\\,x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\n$$\n\nThe function $x=0$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=e.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le e.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/68/680842905f6e308d3c438063769bde9854401a300371452d1c0735bb7d272a02.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=0$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1.$ So, we have $0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\\}.\n$$" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429976 1058 #edb/ref 17592186429978 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429976 1062 #uuid "3390ee50-86eb-5461-9633-3fe230269903" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429976 1063 #edb/ref 17592186429975 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429977 1058 #edb/ref 17592186429980 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429977 1062 #uuid "4eb88ece-6f0a-54bd-b308-acf69dcf4cf6" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429977 1063 #edb/ref 17592186339069 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429978 1062 #uuid "89758ef5-24c5-59a5-a86a-6a96520e9970" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429978 1063 #edb/ref 17592186389594 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429979 1058 #edb/ref 17592186429977 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429979 1062 #uuid "8bd0027a-2407-5324-8c03-911f21cc41f4" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429979 1063 #edb/ref 17592186429974 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429980 1058 #edb/ref 17592186429976 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429980 1062 #uuid "ad81c404-9fb0-5596-9d64-58c400c8f6c0" 13194139534628 17592186045417 true] [17592186429980 1063 #edb/ref 17592186339071 13194139534628 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-d57582b7-233f-54ba-bba8-bc7760d18c20" 17592186429961 "answer-177be529-dbfe-5550-a65b-a03b4c722a7b" 17592186429962 "answer-1ad9fabe-6ac2-5a64-ad33-5fdd7127093f" 17592186429963 "answer-1d70f35